                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.11/792: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >MacMurray</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-05-04T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 4, 1928—6
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>146. Your 295, May 2, 11 a.m., last paragraph. Mission Board states it has
                    telegraphed Doctor Gaston, Laichowfu, to follow Consul’s advice and
                    withdraw.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
